Indicator Diagnostic Considerations and Historical Boundaries
The diagnostic indicator enforces chronological indexing via ArraySetAsSeries(..., false) in OnCalculate(). The initial warm-up segment prior to InpBaselinePeriod is explicitly filled with EMPTY_VALUE to prevent zero-line artifacts on the chart.
The subwindow plot visualizes historical bar spread data (spread[]) from completed bars, while the live dashboard monitors tick-level metrics via SymbolInfoTick() and SYMBOL_SPREAD. Consequently, the indicator's Statistical Dynamic Ceiling plot serves strictly as a historical visual reference calculated from bar spreads, rather than the actual runtime threshold used by CExecutionFilter, whose internal rolling baseline is updated exclusively with approved tick-level spread observations.
Expert Advisor Integration Template
To demonstrate integration and produce verifiable telemetry, we implement EA_Filter_Demo.mq5. The Expert Advisor evaluates candidate entries at the open of each new bar through CExecutionFilter using demonstration settings of 0.10 lot and a 5-bar holding period (InpHoldingBars = 5). In ManageOpenPositions(), the EA checks both the return value of PositionClose() and the server return code (TRADE_RETCODE_DONE) so that a new position cannot be opened while a previous position remains open. Telemetry counters record server dispatch events when requests are transmitted via Buy(), count market executions strictly on TRADE_RETCODE_DONE, and aggregate local request failures or server rejections under orders_rejected.
